// Distortion: the drive current in time, harmonics and THD at 1 kHz, 100 kHz and
// 1 MHz, into the largest drive impedance (1.3 kohm m: R_TRANSFER 11 kohm, contacts
// 77 kohm, about 160 kohm between HC and LC) and into moist loam (100 ohm m: 800 ohm,
// about 12 kohm), SoilModel at relative permittivity 25. The op-amp models are linear
// except for their transient limits (parts/analog_*: output swing from the rails, slew
// rate, output current for the ADA4817 and AD8130), so any harmonic here comes from
// clipping or slewing. The DDS runs at its nominal 0.3 V peak (0.15 V after the filter,
// 15 uA) and, into the largest drive impedance, at 0.65 V, the top of the AD9833's
// output range (README.md, "Structure"), which a wrong setting could produce.
//
// Each run starts in the periodic steady state of the drive (steady = F_DRIVE: found
// by shooting, so the coupling networks do not have to settle over tens of periods)
// and records two periods of it at about 200 samples per period. Into moist loam the
// steps stay uniform and harmonics are established down to about 3e-7 of the
// fundamental (-130 dBc, the integration floor the spectrum plot shades); into the
// driest soil the error control shortens some steps and the floor is 2e-4 (-74 dBc):
// the THD of about 1e-5 at the nominal drive there is integration error (with
// max_step = 1us it is 4e-8 at 1 kHz). Reported without limits: SPEC.md sets no
// distortion requirement (the firmware's I/Q demodulation takes the fundamental).
// Headroom is the pump output's distance from its clipping level (VP less 0.08 V);
// the slew rate needed is 2 pi f times the pump output's peak.
bench Distortion for AnalogFrontEnd using FrontEndPorts, SoilModel, FirmwareReadout {
    param F_DRIVE = 1kHz;
    param A_DDS = 0.3V;
    param T_STOP = 2ms;
    param T_STEP = 5us;
    model DDS: source {
        out = DDS_OUT; ref = GND; ac = 0.3V; output_resistance = 200ohm;
        waveform = sine { amplitude = A_DDS; frequency = F_DRIVE; };
    }

    analysis tran { stop = T_STOP; max_step = T_STEP; steady = F_DRIVE; }
    // About 200 samples per period; two periods recorded.
    step F_DRIVE, T_STOP, T_STEP in (1kHz, 2ms, 5us), (100kHz, 20us, 50ns), (1MHz, 2us, 5ns);
    // Zipped: the largest drive impedance at the nominal and the largest DDS amplitude,
    // moist loam at the nominal amplitude.
    step R_TRANSFER, A_DDS in (11kohm, 0.3V), (11kohm, 0.65V), (800ohm, 0.3V);

    measure current_fundamental = harmonic(i_lc, F_DRIVE, 1);
    measure current_thd = thd(i_lc, F_DRIVE);
    measure current_h2 = harmonic(i_lc, F_DRIVE, 2) / harmonic(i_lc, F_DRIVE, 1);
    measure current_h3 = harmonic(i_lc, F_DRIVE, 3) / harmonic(i_lc, F_DRIVE, 1);
    measure current_sfdr = sfdr(i_lc, F_DRIVE);
    measure pump_output_peak = max(abs(V(DRIVE)));
    measure pump_headroom = 4.42V - max(abs(V(DRIVE)));
    measure slew_needed = 6.2831853 * F_DRIVE * max(abs(V(DRIVE)));
    measure gain1_thd = thd(V(V_MON_1), F_DRIVE);
    measure gain10_thd = thd(V(V_MON_10), F_DRIVE);
    measure current_channel_thd = thd(V(I_MON), F_DRIVE);
    plot i_lc, V(DRIVE), V(PUMP), V(V_MON_1);
    plot spectrum(i_lc, F_DRIVE);
}
